---

{% include "landing/nav.njk" %}

<main class="page-main page-overlay-shelf">
    <div class="container">
        <nav class="page-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span>Overlay Shelf</span>
        </nav>

        <header class="shelf-hero-split">
            <div class="shelf-hero-copy">
                <div class="section-label">Downloads</div>
                <h1 class="shelf-hero-title">Overlay Shelf</h1>
                <p class="shelf-hero-lead">
                    Browser download, then unzip into Foundry's Data folder. Open packs download for anyone.
                    Member and Initiate packs unlock after Connect Patreon. Nothing on this page installs files from inside Foundry.
                </p>
                <div class="shelf-hero-actions">
                    <div class="shelf-hero-cta">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="download-selected-btn" disabled title="Overlays-only zip assemble is next">
                            Download selected overlays
                        </button>
                        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#install">Where files go</a>
                        <span id="shelf-auth-slot" class="shelf-auth-slot"></span>
                    </div>
                    <label class="shelf-check shelf-check--inline">
                        <input type="checkbox" id="include-generative-toggle">
                        <span>Include generative packs</span>
                    </label>
                </div>
                <p class="shelf-note shelf-hero-hint" id="download-selected-hint">
                    Per-pack Download works now. A single overlays-only zip for your selection is next.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="shelf-hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
                <img src="/img/shelf/header.jpg" alt="" width="720" height="405" decoding="async">
            </div>
        </header>

        <section class="shelf-section shelf-section--tight" aria-labelledby="shelf-packs-heading">
            <div class="shelf-section-head">
                <h2 id="shelf-packs-heading" class="shelf-h2">Overlays</h2>
                <p class="shelf-note">Select downloadable packs for the coming combined zip, or download a single pack now. Connect Patreon to unlock member packs.</p>
                <p class="shelf-note shelf-note--disclosure">
                    Some overlays include generative art or audio. Packs without that badge are data or plugins only.
                    Generative packs start unselected; use Include generative packs next to Download selected, or tick individual tiles.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div id="shelf-overlays" aria-live="polite">
                <p class="shelf-loading">Loading pack list...</p>
            </div>
        </section>

                <section class="shelf-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
            <h2 id="install-heading" class="shelf-h2">Where <code>ionrift-data</code> lives</h2>
            <p class="shelf-note">
                Foundry's <strong>Data</strong> folder is the root. Create <code>ionrift-data</code> next to <code>modules</code> and <code>worlds</code> if it is not there yet.
                Unzip so each pack's <code>overlay-manifest.json</code> sits in its subfolder, then reload the world.
            </p>

            <div class="shelf-fs-grid">
                <figure class="shelf-fs-panel">
                    <figcaption>Before</figcaption>
                    <pre class="shelf-fs-tree" aria-label="Data folder before overlays">Data/
|-- modules/
|-- systems/
|-- worlds/
|-- (no ionrift-data yet)</pre>
                </figure>
                <figure class="shelf-fs-panel shelf-fs-panel--after">
                    <figcaption>After (example)</figcaption>
                    <pre class="shelf-fs-tree" aria-label="Data folder after overlays">Data/
|-- modules/
|-- systems/
|-- worlds/
|-- ionrift-data/
    |-- overlays/
        |-- ionrift-respite/
        |   |-- core/
        |   |   |-- overlay-manifest.json
        |   |-- cooking/
        |       |-- overlay-manifest.json
        |-- ionrift-quartermaster/
            |-- core/
                |-- overlay-manifest.json</pre>
                </figure>
            </div>

            <ul class="shelf-host-notes">
                <li><strong>Self-hosted:</strong> open the Foundry User Data path from Setup, or your host's file browser for that volume.</li>
                <li><strong>Hosted Foundry:</strong> use the host's asset / file manager and place the same folder tree under Data.</li>
                <li><strong>Combined zip (soon):</strong> overlays only. Extract at the Data root so <code>ionrift-data/overlays/...</code> lands correctly. Module zips stay separate.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="shelf-card shelf-card--confirm" id="shelf-confirm" aria-labelledby="shelf-confirm-heading">
            <img class="shelf-card-icon" src="/img/shelf/icon-confirm.svg" alt="" width="40" height="40">
            <div class="shelf-card-body">
                <h2 id="shelf-confirm-heading" class="shelf-card-title">Confirm</h2>
                <p class="shelf-note">
                    Paste this Script macro into Foundry and run it to verify overlays on disk
                    (latest / outdated / missing).
                </p>
                <details class="shelf-macro-details">
                    <summary>Show status macro</summary>
                    <pre class="shelf-macro" id="shelf-macro-display" hidden><code></code></pre>
                </details>
                <script type="text/plain" id="shelf-macro-source">/* Ionrift overlay status check */
(async () => {
  const STATUS_URL = "https://api.ionrift.cloud/packs/status";
  const SHELF_URL = "https://ionrift.cloud/overlay-shelf/";

  const compare = (a, b) => {
    const pa = String(a || "0").split(".").map((n) => parseInt(n, 10) || 0);
    const pb = String(b || "0").split(".").map((n) => parseInt(n, 10) || 0);
    const len = Math.max(pa.length, pb.length);
    for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) {
      const d = (pa[i] || 0) - (pb[i] || 0);
      if (d) return d < 0 ? -1 : 1;
    }
    return 0;
  };

  const esc = (value) => String(value ?? "")
    .replace(/&/g, "&amp;")
    .replace(/</g, "&lt;")
    .replace(/>/g, "&gt;")
    .replace(/"/g, "&quot;");

  let listing;
  try {
    const res = await fetch(STATUS_URL, { cache: "no-store" });
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
    listing = await res.json();
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("Ionrift status: failed to fetch listing", err);
    ui.notifications?.error?.("Ionrift status: could not reach the status listing.");
    return;
  }

  const missing = [];
  const outdated = [];
  const current = [];
  const other = [];
  const FP = foundry.applications?.apps?.FilePicker?.implementation ?? FilePicker;

  // Browse first so missing packs do not spam the console with fetch 404s.
  const readLocalVersion = async (installPath) => {
    const dir = String(installPath || "").replace(/\\/g, "/").replace(/\/+$/, "");
    if (!dir) return null;
    try {
      const browse = await FP.browse("data", dir);
      const files = browse?.files || [];
      const manifestUrl = files.find((f) => String(f).endsWith("overlay-manifest.json"));
      if (!manifestUrl) return null;
      const res = await fetch(manifestUrl, { cache: "no-store" });
      if (!res.ok) return null;
      const raw = await res.json();
      return raw?.version || raw?.overlayVersion || null;
    } catch (_) {
      return null;
    }
  };

  for (const row of listing.overlays || []) {
    const path = row.installPath;
    if (!path) {
      other.push(`${row.id}: no install path in listing`);
      continue;
    }

    const local = await readLocalVersion(path);

    if (!local) {
      missing.push(`${row.id}: missing (latest ${row.latest})`);
    } else if (compare(local, row.latest) < 0) {
      outdated.push(`${row.id}: outdated (installed ${local}, latest ${row.latest})`);
    } else if (compare(local, row.latest) > 0) {
      other.push(`${row.id}: newer than listing (installed ${local}, listing ${row.latest})`);
    } else {
      current.push(`${row.id}: at latest (${local})`);
    }
  }

  const lines = [...missing, ...outdated, ...other, ...current];
  console.group("Ionrift overlay status");
  for (const line of lines) console.log(line);
  console.log(`Updates: ${SHELF_URL}`);
  console.groupEnd();

  const section = (title, items, tone) => {
    if (!items.length) return "";
    const lis = items.map((line) => `<li>${esc(line)}</li>`).join("");
    return `<h3 style="margin:0.35em 0 0.35em;font-size:1em;color:${tone}">${esc(title)}</h3><ul style="margin:0;padding-left:1.2em">${lis}</ul>`;
  };

  const content = `
    <div class="ionrift-overlay-status">
      ${section("Missing", missing, "#b91c1c")}
      ${section("Outdated", outdated, "#b45309")}
      ${section("Notes", other, "#52525b")}
      ${section("At latest", current, "#166534")}
      <p style="margin:0.85em 0 0;font-size:0.9em;opacity:0.85">Updates: ${esc(SHELF_URL)}</p>
    </div>
  `;

  new Dialog({
    title: "Ionrift overlay status",
    content,
    buttons: {
      shelf: {
        icon: '<i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i>',
        label: "Open Overlay Shelf",
        callback: () => window.open(SHELF_URL, "_blank", "noopener"),
      },
      close: {
        icon: '<i class="fas fa-check"></i>',
        label: "Close",
      },
    },
    default: "close",
  }).render(true);
})();</script>
            </div>
            <div class="shelf-card-action">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="copy-macro-btn">Copy macro</button>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="shelf-card shelf-card--modules" aria-labelledby="modules-strip-heading">
            <img class="shelf-card-icon" src="/img/shelf/icon-modules.svg" alt="" width="40" height="40">
            <div class="shelf-card-body">
                <h2 id="modules-strip-heading" class="shelf-card-title">Foundry modules by Ionrift Workshop</h2>
                <p class="shelf-note">
                    Cursewright and Monstrous Feast are module zips. Install through Foundry Add-on Modules.
                    They are not part of an overlays zip. Support development on Patreon.
                </p>
                <div id="shelf-modules" class="shelf-module-links" aria-live="polite">
                    <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ site.patreonUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Patreon modules</a>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="shelf-card-action">
                <a class="shelf-patreon-chip" href="{{ site.patreonUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    <svg class="shelf-patreon-chip-logo" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15.386.524c-4.764 0-8.64 3.876-8.64 8.64 0 4.75 3.876 8.613 8.64 8.613 4.75 0 8.614-3.864 8.614-8.613C24 4.4 20.136.524 15.386.524zM.003 23.537h4.22V.524H.003z"/></svg>
                    <span>patreon.com/Ionrift</span>
                    <svg class="shelf-patreon-chip-ext" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6"/><path d="M10 14L20 4"/><path d="M20 14v5a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H5a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V5a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5"/></svg>
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <p class="page-back">
            <a href="/overlays/">&larr; Overlay catalogue</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</main>

